  "description": "The two trivial rules a real model has to beat (ROADMAP item 57). Persistence repeats the last observation available at issuance; climatology is the trailing base rate over the record STRICTLY BEFORE the issuance date. Neither may ever see the day it is forecasting \u2014 a baseline that could peek would score near-perfectly and make every real model look hopeless, and nothing about the page would look broken. A climatology tie breaks DRY, because that is the direction that does not manufacture a rain expectation out of a coin flip. Averages skip missing values rather than counting them as zero.",
